      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Strohmandeln",
          "subtitle": "Austrian tarock game",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Strohmandeln is a two-player Austrian tarock game in the Industrie und Glueck family. It uses a 54-card deck and distinctive strawman packets that create open and hidden information shifts through the deal."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Strohmandeln appears in tarot-family references as a regional tarock game in the broader Industrie und Glueck tradition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two players face each other with strawman packets and hand cards."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "54-card Industrie und Glück pack with 22 permanent trumps and 32 suited cards."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tarock deck and score tracking."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Cards are dealt with a talon packet according to local rules before contract decisions and trick play."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Variations",
          "subtitle": "Known ways this game changes",
          "content": [
            {
